1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,555
This is Release Evidence Desk,
an independent concept by Ayo Ahmed.

2
00:00:04,615 --> 00:00:09,739
Everything here is synthetic. Nothing connects
to Salesforce, and nothing is deployed.

3
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:13,731
I load the seed release,
and four fixed checks run in the browser.

4
00:00:14,041 --> 00:00:17,913
The AI-assisted Agentforce agent
passed its demo, but it's blocked.

5
00:00:17,973 --> 00:00:22,349
It needs an Apex class and a field that aren't
in the slice, or in the target org.

6
00:00:22,659 --> 00:00:27,670
Every finding opens its evidence.
The graph shows both missing pieces in red.

7
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:31,735
It also grants Modify All on Case,
which bypasses sharing.

8
00:00:31,795 --> 00:00:35,675
That's protected.
There's no sign-off button, only a fix.

9
00:00:35,983 --> 00:00:43,433
Revision two is a pre-written fix. It adds the missing pieces,
narrows access to Read, and adds refusal and permission tests.

10
00:00:43,493 --> 00:00:47,096
The blockers clear.
Two access increases still need a human.

11
00:00:47,406 --> 00:00:51,016
I sign off each access increase
with a name and a reason.

12
00:00:51,076 --> 00:00:53,027
A short reason is refused.

13
00:00:53,087 --> 00:00:57,596
Each sign-off is bound to this exact revision.
Change the slice, and it drops.

14
00:01:01,236 --> 00:01:03,239
The slice is now ready to promote.

15
00:01:03,549 --> 00:01:06,967
Compare puts revision one beside revision two,
gate by gate.

16
00:01:07,276 --> 00:01:14,329
Now a blocked exception. This human-authored slice
deletes a field holding 3,412 records.

17
00:01:14,389 --> 00:01:20,219
That deletion is protected. It can't be signed off,
so it's held back while the other three changes ship.

18
00:01:20,531 --> 00:01:25,790
Finally, I export the decision memo: what ships,
what's held back, and who signed off.

19
00:01:26,101 --> 00:01:29,496
It records a decision with evidence.
It never deploys.
